      cells: "....K.",
      note: "NYISO-EXCLUSIVE. A construction-consistency flag, not a lever: when nyiso_dynamic_reserve_requirements enforces a MEASURED hourly requirement on the balance RHS, the ORDC demand curve priced against it is still built off the STATIC published MW, so a family whose measured requirement exceeds its published base (SENY 1,800 vs 1,300 MW) prices its shortfall on a curve ~38 % too steep that saturates above zero reserve. This flag scales each dynamic family's width vector by requirement[t]/requirement_static, translating the published curve without touching its requirement-independent penalties. ROW ADDED 2026-08-02 (nyiso-113) — absent from the matrix; never armed. U: default off and untested at ISO scope, BUT NOTE it is already applied family-scoped and unconditionally to li_30min_total by the LI locational ladder (nyiso_li_locational_reserve), deliberately without flipping this global flag, so that arming the LI ladder does not silently re-span SENY's curve too. A future arm of this flag is a SENY-curve change and needs its own pre-registration. SCREENED EX ANTE 2026-08-03 (nyiso-117, NO SOLVE SPENT, cell stays U because nothing was armed): outcome S-OVER, pre-registered in PREREG-nyiso117 section 6 with its OWN kill set so it is never folded into nyiso_nyc_rcpf_step_curve (rule 19 [R-ONE-MECH]). Instrument identical to the NYC screen -- data/raw/NYISO-AS/NYISO_as_da_<year>.csv, SENY-only = DUNWOD minus CAPITL (in East, NOT in SENY). MEASURED: the isolated SENY-only 30-minute adder caps at $23.92/$30.37/$40.00 in 2023/24/25 with 52 hours of 2025 at EXACTLY the published ASM items-2/12 $40 increment and ZERO hours above it in any year -- one atom over a smooth continuum (272/133/510 material hours, 143/104/334 distinct sub-ceiling values), and the modelled $500 base is NEVER reached in 26,301 hours. MODEL: the family prices in 2/0/8 hours at $62.50-$125.00; its very first ramp rung ($500/8 = $62.50) already sits ABOVE the entire measured envelope, so 9 of 10 binding hours are OVER-priced -- the OPPOSITE direction to NYC's under-pricing. SPAN, the defect this flag exists to fix, confirmed independently: the balance RHS carries the measured hourly requirement (mean 1,602/1,594/1,613 MW, max 1,800) while the ORDC widths are built off the static 1,300 MW -- mis-spanned in 69 % of hours, ratio up to 1.385x. INSTRUMENT HONESTY: the screen's intended negative control DEGENERATES on the 30-minute product (the East 30-min adder is identically $0.00 in every hour, so both references agree and the control has no power to discriminate); it is reported as UNINFORMATIVE rather than as a pass, and the reference pair is validated instead on the 10-minute product where east_10min_total does bind and the same pair separates in 4,603/6,993/6,611 hours (max $27.00/$36.05/$46.22). RECORDED, NOT ACTED ON: no parameter introduced, changed or fitted, no solve spent, no lever proposed. results/calibration/nyiso117_seny_rcpf_curve_screen.json, scripts/probes/_nyiso117_seny_rcpf_curve_screen.py, FINDING-nyiso117 section 6. OUTCOME 2026-08-03 (nyiso-118), CELL U -> K, ARMED AND PROMOTED: solved as 2026-08-03-nyiso-118-seny-span against its own same-HEAD zero-delta control 2026-08-03-nyiso-118-control-zerodelta, 2023-2025 in one bundle each (rule 16), pre-registered and PUSHED BEFORE EITHER SOLVE (PREREG-nyiso118-seny-span-2026-08-03.md). ALL SIX GATES PASS AND K-A..K-E ARE SILENT. G1 the construction identity is RESTORED: SENY's total step width differed from its own requirement in 6,239/6,249/6,231 hours of 2023/24/25 in the control and 0/0/0 in the treatment. G2a every family's requirement_mw float32-EXACTLY identical between arms (np.array_equal, not a 1e-6 MW tolerance the float32 dtype cannot represent, nyiso-116). G2c an instrument that never touches the parquet: the solve log's ORDC step count is UNCHANGED at 59/59/59 in BOTH arms -- the flag re-spans widths and adds or removes NO steps -- committed as each bundle's ordc_steps.log. G3/G4/G5/G6 pass with zero slack and zero dump in both arms. THE LI DOUBLE-APPLY HAZARD WAS DISCHARGED EX ANTE, ON CONSTRUCTION, BEFORE THE SOLVE (scripts/probes/_nyiso118_span_construction_probe.py -> results/calibration/nyiso118_span_construction_probe.json): the probe builds the NYISO ReserveDesign TWICE at one HEAD and diffs every family's requirement, ordc_penalties and ordc_step_widths with NO LP and NO dual -- because dual and held_mw are SOLVED co-optimization outputs whose byte-identity can only pass when the mechanism does nothing (the nyiso-115 G2 error). li_30min_total is byte-identical between arms in ALL THREE vectors in all three years: K-A did not fire, because the guard's `or` is boolean rather than additive and LI's family-scoped entry has already normalized its widths. TWO CORRECTIONS TO THE RECORD, both MEASURED rather than assumed. (1) THE BLAST RADIUS IS THREE FAMILIES, NOT ONE: _nyiso_design's docstring claimed a no-op for NYCA, East and NYC, which is FALSE for NYC -- its measured requirement dips BELOW its static base in 185/227/120 hours (mean 490.8 vs 500 MW). Docstring corrected against the probe in the same session. (2) BUT NYC IS RE-REPRESENTED, NOT RE-PRICED, so the rule-23 freeze on nyiso_nyc_rcpf_step_curve is NOT disturbed: shortfall is bounded above by the hour's requirement (held >= 0), so width beyond it is unreachable padding, and under the frozen step curve that family is a SINGLE FLAT BAND at the published $25 RCPF -- trimming padding off a flat band cannot move a price. Reachable price pointwise IDENTICAL ($0.000, 0 hours, all three years), so K-B did not fire. That three-way split -- SENY re-priced, NYC re-represented, LI untouched -- is what demonstrates the construction instrument HAS DISCRIMINATING POWER; it is not a gate that can only pass by doing nothing. THE PARTIAL WAS PRE-REGISTERED AND HELD -- THIS DOES NOT CLOSE S-OVER AND IS NOT REPORTED AS DOING SO: the flag re-spans WIDTHS only, SENY's penalties are measured UNCHANGED, and its FIRST RUNG IS STILL $62.50, already above the ENTIRE measured $23.92/$30.37/$40.00 envelope. The remaining defect (published curve = $500 base PLUS a $40 increment; the model carries only the base as a critical_mw = 0 ramp) is a SECOND mechanism needing its own pre-registration and its own arm (rule 19 [R-ONE-MECH]) and is the NAMED OPEN SUCCESSOR in NYISO's lever queue; nothing was introduced, changed or fitted for it here. MEASURED EFFECT: 2023 and 2024 are BIT-IDENTICAL between arms; only 2025 moves and it moves DOWNWARD -- SENY max dual 125.00 -> 87.07, the shallower ramp and the pre-registered direction. Small because SENY BINDS IN ALMOST NO HOURS (2/0/8), NOT because the curve barely changed: its reachable price differs in ~6,100 hours per year, but a demand curve can only price where there is a shortfall. The NYC pair gains one binding hour each in 2025 with its own curve provably unchanged -- co-optimization general equilibrium propagating through held reserve, which is exactly why the scope kill was written on CONSTRUCTION and the duals REPORTED rather than gated. ALL 18 SCORED NUMERIC FIELDS EQUAL between arms; determination CALIBRATED-WITH-CAVEATS with C3c the sole caveat, UNCHANGED (a null PRE-REGISTERED in prereg section 5). DOF ledger 31 -> 32 entries with n_residual UNCHANGED at 6: the scale factor is the ratio of two already-committed measured inputs and the RCPF penalties are requirement-INDEPENDENT, so there is nothing in the mechanism to tune. PROMOTION RESTS ON RULE 1 [R-STRUCT] / RULE 14 [R-ACCURATE] AND THE RESIDUAL DELIBERATELY DID NOT MOVE -- rule 1 is explicit that a structurally-correct mechanism is never rejected or reverted because the residual didn't move, and the static 1,300 MW span was an ESTIMATE leaking into a curve whose balance row is measured, which is what rule 14 forbids keeping. DO NOT RE-TEST: armed, solved, gated and keeper. FINDING-nyiso118-seny-span-2026-08-03.md.",
