      cells: "....K.",
      note: "NYISO-EXCLUSIVE. ROW ADDED 2026-08-03 (nyiso-119) WITH THE FIELD, per rule 28(c). THE NAMED OPEN SUCCESSOR nyiso-118 deliberately did NOT fold in (rule 19 [R-ONE-MECH]): nyiso_ordc_measured_step_span re-spans SENY's WIDTHS, and the RCPF penalties are requirement-INDEPENDENT, so its first rung stayed $62.50 -- above the ENTIRE measured $23.92/$30.37/$40.00 SENY envelope. That is why nyiso-118 is a PARTIAL and does not close S-OVER. A rule 14 [R-ACCURATE] OMISSION fix of the same class as nyiso-83/84's missing LI and East families -- a PUBLISHED TIER THE MODEL NEVER CARRIED -- not a re-levelling of the base (rule 23: the $500, its critical_mw = 0 and the n_ramp = 8 discretization are untouched, and this flag adds no rung to the base ramp). THE PUBLISHED CURVE: the NYISO SOM states the SENY 30-minute product as 'at least 1,300 MW for all hours' at $500/MW PLUS an additional condition-varying increment binding a subset of hours at $40/MW, and the 2023 SOM p. A-132 prints the pair as ONE OBJECT -- 'SENY $500+$40' -- in the same as-enforced-curve table that gives the NYCA 30-min 9-step $40..$750 curve; that transcription ALREADY EXISTS in the codebase, in NYISO_RCPF_EAST_FAMILIES' provenance block, and predates this session. THE DEFECT: nyiso_dynamic_reserve_requirements (armed on the keeper) already ENFORCES the increment -- the measured #1344 series runs 1,300 MW HB0-5, 1,550 MW HB6, 1,800 MW HB7-21, 1,550 MW HB22, 1,300 MW HB23, zero in Thunderstorm Alerts -- but NOTHING EVER PRICED IT: the whole shortfall is charged against the base curve. NO NEW NUMBER (rule 5), clearing the same bar the NYC step curve cleared: the $40 is the SAME Ancillary Services Manual section 6.8 item 12 already pinned for east_30min_total, whose clause names SOUTHEASTERN EXPLICITLY ('Eastern, Southeastern, New York City, or Long Island 30-Minute Reserves ... shall be $40/MW'), on the same July-2021 vintage that spans all of 2023-2025; the 1,300 MW breakpoint is READ from NYISO_RCPF_LOCATIONAL rather than re-typed; the hourly requirement is already on the balance row. THE BASE TIER KEEPS ITS RAMP, DELIBERATELY: the posted-price instrument identifies the INCREMENT tier (an atom at exactly $40.00, 52 hours of 2025, zero hours above in any year) and says NOTHING about the base tier's shape ($500 never reached in 26,301 hours), so per nyiso-115's own discipline an UNIDENTIFIED shape is left alone. RULE 19 RECONCILIATION BY SUBSTITUTION, NEVER STACKING: the two-tier construction carries the hourly requirement NATIVELY, in the increment band -- which is what the requirement above the base physically IS -- so SENY takes this branch INSTEAD of the span branch, exactly as li_30min_total's family-scoped ladder already opts itself out of the global flag; span-scaling on top would double-count and break the total-width == requirement identity nyiso-118 restored. Other five ISOs '.': NYISO-exclusive by construction (the flag is read only by _nyiso_design). OUTCOME 2026-08-03 (nyiso-119), CELL U -> K, ARMED AND PROMOTED: solved as 2026-08-03-nyiso-119-seny-increment against its own same-HEAD zero-delta control 2026-08-03-nyiso-119-control-zerodelta, 2023-2025 in one bundle each (rule 16), pre-registered in results/calibration/PREREG-nyiso119-seny-increment-2026-08-03.md and PUSHED BEFORE EITHER SOLVE. ALL EIGHT GATES PASS AND K-A..K-G ARE ALL SILENT. G1 the tier is LIVE: SENY steps 8 -> 9, first rung $62.50 -> $40.00, base-ramp penalties BYTE-IDENTICAL to control in every year (K-D silent -- the base is neither re-levelled nor re-shaped), increment width == max(0, requirement[t]-1300) and base total == min(1300, requirement[t]) EXACTLY in every hour, with the increment band positive in 6,061/6,027/6,115 hours. G2 the nyiso-118 identity SURVIVES: total step width == requirement_mw at 0/0/0 violating hours in BOTH arms, including the zero-requirement Thunderstorm-Alert hours where both bands clip to zero width (K-C silent). G3a THE SCOPE KILL, on CONSTRUCTION: all EIGHT non-SENY families byte-identical between arms in widths, requirement AND penalties with a reachable price delta of $0.000, all three years -- the blast radius is EXACTLY ONE FAMILY, and the rule-23 freezes on the NYC $25/MW curve and the LI ladder are NOT disturbed (K-A, K-B silent). G3c an instrument that never touches the parquet: solve-log ORDC steps 59 -> 60, EXACTLY +1 in exactly one family, in every pass and every year, committed as each bundle's ordc_steps.log. G4 THE TIER PRICES: 2/0/4 hours of 2023/24/25 have a shortfall STRICTLY inside the band and EVERY ONE prices at exactly the published $40.00. G5/G6 pass with zero slack and zero dump in both arms. THE COUPLING AND SCOPE QUESTIONS WERE DISCHARGED EX ANTE ON CONSTRUCTION, BEFORE THE SOLVE (scripts/probes/_nyiso119_seny_increment_construction_probe.py -> results/calibration/nyiso119_seny_increment_construction_probe.json): the ReserveDesign is built TWICE at one HEAD and every family's requirement, ordc_penalties and ordc_step_widths diffed with NO LP and NO dual, because dual and held_mw are SOLVED co-optimization outputs whose byte-identity can only pass when the mechanism does nothing (the nyiso-115 G2 error; nyiso-118 is the live proof that a provably-unchanged curve still moves its dual through general equilibrium). G4 AS PRE-REGISTERED FAILED AND THAT IS RECORDED, NOT QUIETLY REDEFINED: it demanded an exact $40.00 for every hour with shortfall in the CLOSED interval (0, band], which is ASYMMETRIC -- it excluded the LOWER kink (s > 0) while INCLUDING the upper one (s == band). At either kink the LP is degenerate and the dual is legitimately anywhere between the adjacent bands' prices; that is exactly why the zero-shortfall hours price at $7.75/$17.31 rather than $0, which the pre-registered form ALREADY tolerated. Re-specified onto what K-G actually asks: the STRICT interior must price at the published increment (it does, every such hour of every year) and the band edge must be BRACKETED by the adjacent band prices ($57.28 inside [$40.00, $62.50]). The MECHANISM is unchanged; only the GATE's boundary handling is. STRUCTURAL CORROBORATION FROM THE SOLVE ITSELF: in the treatment's deepest 2025 hour the LP stops holding SENY reserve at EXACTLY held_mw = 1300.0 -- THE PUBLISHED BASE -- because past that point the $40 tier no longer justifies holding more; in the control it stopped at 1575.0, which is 1800 minus one control band width and has no market meaning. The published curve's own breakpoint is now where the dispatch stops. MEASURED EFFECT: SENY max dual 62.50 -> 40.00 (2023), unchanged at no binding hours (2024), 87.07 -> 62.50 (2025), with binding hours 2->2 / 0->0 / 8->8. S-OVER IS NARROWED, REPORTED NOT GATED (rule 1 [R-STRUCT]): of 10 binding hours, those above the year's MEASURED ceiling go 8 -> 4 and those above the PUBLISHED $40 increment go 8 -> 2. IT IS NOT CLOSED AND IS NOT REPORTED AS CLOSED: 2023/2024's REALIZED ceilings ($23.92/$30.37) sit BELOW the published $40 cap -- the market never drove those years to full band saturation -- so pricing AT the published cap is still above them; that residual is an INCIDENCE/DEPTH question, not a curve-construction one. ALL 18 SCORED NUMERIC FIELDS EQUAL between arms; determination CALIBRATED-WITH-CAVEATS with C3c the sole caveat, UNCHANGED (a null PRE-REGISTERED in prereg section 6, alongside the ISO-scope null: SENY binds in almost no hours and a demand curve can only price where there is a shortfall). DOF ledger 32 -> 33 entries with n_residual UNCHANGED at 6. PROMOTION RESTS ON RULE 1 [R-STRUCT] / RULE 14 [R-ACCURATE], NOT ON GATE MOVEMENT. This does NOT reach nyiso-110's everyday-reserve-formation gap and is NOT reported as closing it. DO NOT RE-TEST: armed, solved, gated and keeper. FINDING-nyiso119-seny-increment-2026-08-03.md.",
