      cells: "K.....",
      note: "Row added 2026-08-02 (ercot-151) as a rule-28(c) repair — the flag predates the matrix guard and had no row. ERCOT-88 built and merged it default-off: OFF-status fast-start CT rows (physics gate min_down <= FASTSTART_POOL_MIN_DOWN_HOURS, never a class tuple) take the pool's measured start-inclusive above-LSL SCED2 ladder (p50 $271-707, p90 $641-1010 by net-load bin, 2024), REPLACE-BY-MASK over the other surfaces (rule 19), an offer-availability never a floor. As a CT-only slice the LP CLEARED AROUND it on the un-repriced cheap CC offline block, so it never moved the tail; ERCOT-107/108's scope correction chartered the widening (re-price the offline increment, never cap it — the rejected ercot41/43 envelope family stays closed) and ercot-151 Phase 0 measured the object on the ercot150b keeper's own 91 missed 2023 >$300 hours (model $105 vs actual $860): 18.1 GW config-collapsed startable-but-OFF CC+CT (CC 10.3 / CT 7.8) vs 14.5 GW ON, ~13.5 GW of the increment at submitted-DAM <= $200 — the phantom cheap DEPTH that caps the model against a ~0.5 GW cushion. Cell O: the CC(+ST) slow-start tier widening + the pool's missing 2023 year block are the chartered arm (DIAGNOSIS-ercot151-offline-increment-phase0-2026-08-02.md section 3), DATA-BLOCKED on an owner re-upload of the NP3-965 corpus (purged 2026-07-22 by the large-blob history rewrite; free-path retention starts ~2024-01) and owner-gated (ERCOT-89 section 7 step 2). Constants-based startup amortization ($20-30/MWh) is refuted ex ante as the identification — 30x below the measured conduct ladder. ercot-152 (2026-08-02, owner directed proceed-without-corpus; committed-data census scripts/probes/ercot152_cc_tier_census.py -> results/calibration/ercot152_cc_tier_census.json): the CC WIDENING REFUSES EX ANTE on the corpus's own evidence — CC OFFQS/OFFNS is ~0 MW in all four committed extracts (no measured object for the ERCOT-88 construction), and plain-OFF CC's own disclosed SCED2 curves are CHEAP (above-LSL MW-weighted p50 $19.5-34.7 / p90 $57.5-97.7, near the ON fleet's +$7-12), so re-pricing the offline CC increment at 'its true start-inclusive offer' is a measured NO-OP — the CC block's phantom depth is a COMMITMENT-STATE gap whose cap-side expression is the closed ercot41/43/106/108 envelope family. DO NOT build a CC tier from this corpus. The full-corpus re-upload ask now buys primarily the 2023 CT-pool YEAR BLOCK (CT OFFQS/OFFNS conduct is real and high-priced); it remains owner-declined 2026-08-02 (repo-size risk after the history rewrite). RESOLVED 2026-08-03 (ercot-157): the owner re-uploaded the delivery-2023 corpus to data/raw/ercot/SCED/ (315 shards, verified complete — all 365 delivery days), and the pool's 2023 CT year block is derived and committed alongside the CC/CT wall's 2023 full-year refresh (the committed block had been the Jan-Oct post-purge slice; tail bins 5-6 byte-identical). O -> I at ercot-158 (2026-08-03, the owner-authorized ERCOT-89 section 7 step-2 arming round, ERCOT-151 section 4 ask 2): full-span single-delta A/B off the ercot150b keeper (arm 2026-08-03-ercot158-pool-arm vs same-HEAD honest-inputs control 2026-08-03-ercot158-honest-replay; PRECOMMIT + kill gates pushed before either arm solved). The pool ENGAGED all three years (173/173/91 rows; 2025 matches the ERCOT-88 record) and is INERT at its target: the keeper's 91 missed 2023 >$300 hours are BIT-IDENTICAL between arms (missed-set model mean $105.163 -> $105.163, 0 flips) — the marginal unit at those hours is never a pool-owned CT row; the un-repriced cheap CC offline block (~8 GW <=$200; the ERCOT-152 measured-no-op refusal, upheld) keeps the cushion, exactly the Phase-0 arithmetic. All pre-registered gates HELD every year (zero spurious, tail counts identical, NRMSE 2.870->2.866 best delta); scorecard 73 verdict rows zero PASS->FAIL; D-2 sets identical with zero forced-energy delta (offer-availability confirmed vacuous). Only measurable motion: slight 2023 softening (hit-set mean -$16) where the pool ladder REPLACES a higher wall markup — structurally honest, direction DOWN. DISPOSITION I -> K same session: OWNER-PROMOTED KEEPER 2026-08-03-ercot158-pool-arm under the standing standard ('If structural integrity improves but gates regress that may still be a keeper') on the session's YES recommendation — the promotion rests on the IDENTIFICATION (rule 1: ERCOT-87 adjudicated that the real mid-band prices on the offline startable CT pool, so an online-basis wall price on those rows is refuted by status; arming prices that capability at measured conduct), NOT on the inert-at-target A/B, which is recorded verbatim: the 91 missed 2023 >$300 hours are bit-identical between arms and the 2023 tail residual is a COMMITMENT-STATE gap (the CC offline block's phantom cheap depth), successor per DIAGNOSIS-ercot151 section 3 / ercot-152. Rubric cost REPORTED: C3a 2023 -32.6 -> -32.8% (-0.2pp); every criterion status identical to ercot150b. Other ISOs '.': no comparable RT offline-conduct disclosure instrument.",
