      cells: "K.....",
      note: "ERCOT KEEPER at ERCOT-149 — OWNER-PROMOTED 2026-08-01 (the session registered the arm as a KEEPER CANDIDATE and reserved the disposition on the tripped spurious guard; the owner promoted on the standing standard 'if structural integrity improves but gates regress that may still be a keeper'): keeper 2026-08-01-ercot149-gas-event-cap, bundle ercot149_gas_event_cap_arm. ERCOT-149 (2026-08-01, the ERCOT-148 named successor / open owner ruling #7). Phase 0/1 no-LP audit (docs/DIAGNOSIS-ercot149-gas-cop-window-2026-08-01.md; committed record results/calibration/ercot149_gas_outage_phase0.json; probe scripts/probes/ercot149_gas_outage_phase0.py): the keeper dispatches 4.27/5.93/4.14 TWh (2023/24/25) of CC_REGULAR + ST_GAS above the measured event-window ceiling — same order as the coal phantom ERCOT-148 removed — decoded from the keeper payload (machinery verified by reproducing the committed coal 4.36/4.98/5.01 per plant to 0.01 TWh on the prior payload). The coal ruling did NOT transfer by assumption; the gas adjudication rests on the gas fleet's own conduct: (a) the windows are event-based dead spans (every hour < 2% CF) that survived the armed merit-order guard, and 81.6% of their GW-days sit at exactly 0.0 out-of-merit share (in merit for weeks while producing nothing — layup untenable, mechanical); (b) the mapped-channel restore decomposes into MEASURED site-series misalignments — config-collapse train-aliasing (GUADG/KMCHI: _site() folds two physical CC trains into one site, live = max across trains, so a single-train outage is invisible EVEN WITH honest OUT filings — the largest single case, Guadalupe Oct-Dec 2024, is erased despite COP OUT), partial site acceptance (JACKCNTY covers train 1 only, train 2 is unaccepted site JCKCNTY2; BRAUNIG_VHB3/GIDEONG3/OLING_3/SANDHSYD/DANSBYG1 subsets), and true OFF-at-HSL through certified dead stops at covered sites (BASTEN, NUECES_B — the Coleto/Limestone conduct on gas); (c) honest-OUT controls carry ~zero phantom (Victoria dam_frac 0.019 -> 0.004 TWh; V H Braunig within-plant 2024 frac 0.70 -> 0.64 TWh vs 2025 frac 0.075 -> 0.06); (d) the unmapped channel (~half) is the class-hour/residual water-fill restoring windowed units; (e) CHP no-overlay controls show true dispatch respects the ceiling (their apparent 0.07-0.24 TWh is the dashboard render's flat BTM adder, verified 39.1 MW at Pasadena 2024). Adjudicated a DEFECT of the ERCOT-148 class: two incumbent measured layers conflict at the seam (both window layers are armed incumbents on gas — arrays.py:1026/:1226 — and the DAM overlay is the only restoring layer above them); rule 14 prefers the physical CEMS record on conflicted hours, rule 19 reconciles via the SAME min() block. Zero fitted parameters. Phase 2 precommit docs/PRECOMMIT-ercot149-dam-gas-event-cap-2026-08-01.md (pushed before the solve), single delta off ercot148_dam_event_cap_arm. *** PHASE 2 SOLVED AND REGISTERED (2026-08-01-ercot149-gas-event-cap, full span, one invocation, seam-verified armed==min(base,ceiling) exactly on all 1,138 scoped tranches): KEEPER CANDIDATE, NOT PROMOTED — TEN OF ELEVEN pre-registered guards HELD, ONE TRIPPED, and the disposition belongs to the owner (the handoff reserves ruling #7 'surface, do not decide'). Held: C3c 2023/2025 tails EXACT (54/0, spurious 2/0 byte-level); C1 16/16 free 12/12 EXACT; C2/C4/C8 PASS; C7-2024/25 lignite both legs PASS (hard kill); n_residual 6; C6 ATTESTED+PASS; determination NOT-YET with fail set {C3a(now 2023-only), C3b(2023-only), C3c, C7(2023-lignite cv-leg)} identical-in-kind to the keeper and SHRINKING. Un-targeted improvements (rule 1 — reported, never the basis): C3a −34.3/−10.4/−11.6 → −33.3/+0.8/−9.1 (2024 FLIPS PASS, essentially exact), C3b 0.618→0.616 / 0.205→0.198 / 0.112 all improve, C3c-2024 formation matched hours 4→13 toward the actual 53 (tail 7→20, 0.13×→0.38×), C7-2023 lignite profile r 0.879→0.886, coal-2024 under-run −8.9% improves (+1.26 TWh PRB). TRIPPED: C3c spurious-2024 3→7 vs the ≤3(+1 straddle) guard. Hour-level anatomy (recorded verbatim, scratch-reproducible from the committed system parquets): 3 of 7 are the KEEPER'S OWN spurious hours byte-carried (Jan-15 Heather morning, prices within $2); 1 is a LITERAL threshold straddle (keeper $199.9 that hour → arm $204.7); the 3 genuinely new are single-hour TRAILING EDGES of REAL events the arm newly forms — Apr-15/Apr-27/May-7 2024 evenings, actual RT peaking $958/$1,260/$3,049 within ±3h, each attached to 2–4 newly MATCHED hours at the same event — event-boundary overhang of real formation, not invented scarcity on quiet days (the guarded failure mode). Adverse un-predicted direction, reported honestly: ST_GAS class energy rose +0.46/+0.26/+0.55 TWh (picked up displaced CC energy; its over-run worsens, inside C1/C2 bands), and the rebuild's [7c] operating-shape report flags cf_emd regressions on CC_REGULAR/COAL/CC_CHP — the substitution margin ran to coal, the OPEN CC-dearness object (ERCOT-138/139), exposed further by removing the phantom. CC_REGULAR −2.15/−3.32/−2.13 TWh (crossed to small under, pre-registered); named plants: Nueces Bay +63/+62/+69% → +64/+49/+49%, Jack County 2024 +3.7%→−13.4% and Guadalupe further under (both pre-registered compensating-error unwinds). Successor root causes surfaced (owner rulings, NOT fixed here): the deriver _site() cross-train max (should sum per-train maxes — rule-23 derive lane), the gas crosswalk's partial site acceptance, and the pin's remove-direction over-removal at partial-coverage plants (V H Braunig 2025), all out of this lane's restore-direction scope.",
